# Spec Writing

When writing or updating specs:

## Format
Use the template at `specs/_template.md`. Include:
- **Overview**: one paragraph — what and why
- **User stories**: As a [role], I want [action], so that [value]
- **Acceptance criteria**: concrete, testable behaviors (user sees X, clicking Y does Z)
- **Edge cases**: empty states, errors, missing data, boundary conditions
- **Out of scope**: what this spec intentionally does NOT cover

## Rules
- Business requirements only — no code, file paths, or implementation details
- Every acceptance criterion must be testable by an automated test
- User-facing text must match the application's language
- For modifications: clearly mark what changed vs what stays the same
- Set status to `draft` — only the developer can approve specs

## After approval
Remind to commit the spec before starting implementation. The `git diff` of the spec commit scopes the implementation work.
